        "motion_energy": 26.85,
        "script": "There are four behaviors that I see of the happiest possible people. These are people who practice their faith or life philosophy seriously. These are people who take care of their family relationships. They're paying attention to their families, not neglecting their families and not having bitterness inside their families. These are people who have real friends, not deal friends. These are people who are doing the work and these are people who are dedicating their work to just two things, earning their success, which is say creating real value and serving other people. That's what they have. And I don't care if they're plumbers or politicians or professors, CEOs or journalists or anything in between, you need to believe that you're doing something that creates value and you're being recognized for it and that you're serving other people. And those are the big four, faith, family, friends and work. Those are the behaviors that will give you better circumstances and allow you to manage your genetics and give you the most happiness that you can possibly get."
